WEBVTT

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:26.450
" <i>The Adventures of Fran</i> "...?

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:34.080
I wonder if it's like <i>The Adventures of Niké</i> ?

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.540
It's not just that the name
is the same as Miss Fran's--

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:41.240
I feel like the face here looks like her, too...

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.910
As I looked at that book,

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:48.580
I remembered a country
I stopped by six months before.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:53.450
It was a big country, far away from here--

00:00:53.450 --> 00:00:57.950
It was called Royal Celesteria.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:41.020
Royal Celesteria

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.240
Oh?

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.080
The mages are doing tricks
for everyone to enjoy.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:12.160
It's wonderful.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:25.870
Put your hands together!

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.290
"Royal Magic Academy"...

00:03:31.290 --> 00:03:33.950
I didn't know they had a place like this...

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.700
I wonder if it's okay to go in?

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:40.370
Probably not, right...?

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:43.410
But... I'll just do it.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.870
Hey!

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.080
No trespassers allowed here!

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:57.080
Oh, I'm sorry. You're a witch?

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:59.160
Please excuse my rude behavior.

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:00.490
Don't worry about it.

00:04:00.490 --> 00:04:02.790
Well then, please excuse me.

00:04:03.950 --> 00:04:06.620
No one is allowed inside without permission.

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.990
Not even witches?

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.660
Not even witches.

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:17.490
He could've at least let me
look around a little bit...

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:20.990
Anyway, I guess I'll look for a place to stay.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.990
Excuse me!

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:31.740
I wonder if that person
is delivering newspapers?

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:39.660
The mages in this country are...

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:45.950
Um, did you need something?

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:49.450
Hello. You're the Ashen Witch, right?

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:54.870
W-We're students at the Royal Magic Academy.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:57.490
Are you students from
the school I was at earlier?

00:04:57.490 --> 00:04:59.240
What business do you have with me?

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:05.540
U-Um, will you come with us
without asking any questions?

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:07.200
Why should I?

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.290
I-I said without asking any questi--

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:10.990
I don't want to.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:13.620
Why not?

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.660
Because I don't want to.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:18.080
Come on, please?

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:21.990
Just trust me and come with us, please.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.790
No way.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:24.950
Later.

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:26.660
Huh?!

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.870
Hey, guys, let's do this as a team.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.540
Yes, let's catch her together.

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:38.410
Catch me? Why?

00:05:38.410 --> 00:05:40.450
Don't take all the glory for yourself!

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:42.040
Speak for yourself!

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:45.660
I don't know what's going on, but...

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.200
Hey, wait up!

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:52.620
The Ashen Witch?

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.740
P-Please don't run away!

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:56.580
You guys go toward the river.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:00.040
And you guys go around
from the state guest house!

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:13.870
Found you, Madam Ashen Witch!

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:16.160
Please come with us quietly!

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.910
They do have the advantage
of knowing the lay of the land.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:42.290
They're stubborn.

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.910
They're determined, at least.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:49.200
Very well. In that case,
I'll see this through to the end.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:54.540
Madam Ashen Witch, I've got you!

00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:55.910
Slip.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.040
Huh?!

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:03.740
You should really open your eyes.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:08.990
Madam Ashen Witch, I've got you!

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:13.740
I-I can't go on...

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.540
I-I'm dying...

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:21.410
You should know by now that you
can't catch me even if you try as a group.

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:23.950
Please give up.

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:24.740
Goodbye.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:28.330
Everyone, good work.

00:07:28.330 --> 00:07:30.580
M-Ma'am...!

00:07:33.540 --> 00:07:37.410
You all had no chance against her, did you?

00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:39.160
N-No...

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.790
Age doesn't matter.

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:46.200
This is the difference between you and a witch.

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:52.200
Long time no see, Elaina.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.160
Miss Fran...

00:07:54.160 --> 00:08:00.830
That was the first time I'd seen
my teacher, Miss Fran, in a few years.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.120
That's it for today's extracurricular lesson.

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:07.370
Please turn in your report tomorrow.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:08.240
Okay...

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:11.240
Thank you very much...

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:15.080
Oh my, they're all so unsteady on their feet.

00:08:15.080 --> 00:08:16.910
Maybe you overdid it a little?

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:19.120
Are you saying it's my fault?

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:21.580
It's also my fault.

00:08:21.580 --> 00:08:25.540
Are you a teacher at this school, Miss Fran?

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:28.950
Yes. The king asked me to teach here.

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:30.990
Well, let's not stand
around here talking all day.

00:08:30.990 --> 00:08:33.580
Let's go inside, Elaina.

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:38.830
As part of their extracurricular lessons,

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:45.370
I told them to bring you to me,
even if they had to use some force.

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:49.700
How did you know that I was in town?

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:53.200
You tried to come into the school, didn't you?

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:56.870
A young witch with
ash-colored hair tried to enter.

00:08:56.870 --> 00:09:00.540
She might be a spy from another country!

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:04.910
A spy? He really jumped to conclusions...

00:09:04.910 --> 00:09:07.200
I knew right away that it was you.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:12.660
Then, I just couldn't sit still,
so I used my students to find you.

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:16.540
I thought it'd be hard to find you
myself in such a big country,

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:20.540
and it would be good training for them.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:26.200
Because going up against
a talented witch is excellent training.

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:29.990
Talented? Well, I guess
you could say that, but...

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:34.410
It was a rare opportunity,
so those kids were happy, too.

00:09:34.410 --> 00:09:37.660
I was, too, though.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:43.580
You've traveled a lot, haven't you?

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.240
Yes.

00:09:45.240 --> 00:09:48.450
You knew that I was traveling?

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:49.490
Of course.

00:09:49.490 --> 00:09:51.040
I heard from your mother.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:53.120
Huh? You've seen her?

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:56.540
She's very worried about you, you know.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:10:00.120
If you're ever near your
hometown, you should go visit.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:01.910
I'm planning to.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.160
Oh, good.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:08.540
So, why did you want to
become a traveler, Elaina?

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.660
I expect it was because of your mother?

00:10:10.660 --> 00:10:12.370
Mom?

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:14.740
Oh, it wasn't?

00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:18.120
It was mainly because of a book
called <i>The Adventures of Niké</i> ,

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:20.080
which I read when I was young.

00:10:20.080 --> 00:10:21.830
Oh, really?

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:24.200
I like that book, too.

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:28.290
My favorite is the last story,
"Foula, the Apprentice Witch."

00:10:28.290 --> 00:10:31.120
That's my favorite, too!

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:33.660
It's the story of how the witch, Niké,

00:10:33.660 --> 00:10:39.240
takes on the apprentice witch,
Foula, and helps her grow.

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:43.700
In the end, Niké lives in the
countryside as an ordinary woman,

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:50.120
and Foula becomes the new traveler
as the curtain falls on Niké's adventures.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.910
That takes me back.

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:53.120
Huh?

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:55.790
Oh, I was talking about this book.

00:10:55.790 --> 00:10:58.450
Just between you and me,

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:05.290
I loved <i>The Adventures of Niké</i> so much
that I wrote a novel as I traveled.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:08.290
Oh, really.

00:11:08.290 --> 00:11:10.740
You don't sound very interested.

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:13.990
No, no, I'm super interested.

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:16.370
And?

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:20.410
After I hit about a hundred pages
of manuscript and went back to read it,

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:23.870
it was so pathetic that it
made me writhe on the floor.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:24.910
Huh.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:30.080
I didn't take it out of my travel bag
after that and forgot about it,

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:34.790
but when I was in a certain
country, I sold my bag.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:39.120
Apparently, that bag was
the bag of a legendary traveler.

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:41.450
A legendary traveler's bag?

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:44.290
It was a cheap bag I'd bought
in a pawnshop, though.

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:48.700
And you left your manuscript in that bag?

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.540
How did you know?

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:53.160
Who <i>wouldn't</i> have been able to figure that out?

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:56.700
I remember it occasionally,
and it makes me so embarrassed.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:12:01.660
What if someone found
the manuscript and read it?

00:12:01.660 --> 00:12:03.490
Miss Fran...

00:12:03.490 --> 00:12:07.080
Anyway, it's something I can laugh about now.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.700
So what was the point of telling me about it?

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:12.370
Isn't it obvious?

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:17.200
A lot of things will happen to you
as you continue on your journey.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:20.910
Someday, I'd like to hear
stories of your fun memories.

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:24.290
Please tell me lots of
stories about your travels.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.910
That's what I wanted to say.

00:12:25.910 --> 00:12:27.740
Very well.

00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.870
Make sure you write in your diary.

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:32.950
You even heard about that from my mom?

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:35.740
I'm looking forward to it--

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:37.370
and so is your mother.

00:12:37.370 --> 00:12:41.240
Then, I can't get lazy about writing in it.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:48.080
Everyone, I believe you met her yesterday,
but let me introduce her again.

00:12:48.080 --> 00:12:50.830
This is the Ashen Witch, Elaina.

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.410
Um, hello.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:56.080
She'll be a special guest lecturer today.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:58.080
Does anyone have any questions for her?

00:12:58.080 --> 00:12:58.990
I do!

00:12:58.990 --> 00:12:59.790
Go ahead.

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:02.240
Do you have a boyfriend? Do you?

00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:04.790
I do not. I'm a traveler after all.

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:07.740
Please keep it to questions about magic.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:09.370
Anyone else?

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:11.950
Um...

00:13:11.950 --> 00:13:16.290
Wh-What kind of magic are you good at?

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:17.910
There's isn't one specific type.

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:20.080
From attack magic to transformation magic,

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:23.120
I feel like I have a good handle
on all kinds of magic.

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:25.410
I-I see...

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:30.330
Of all the countries you've ever visited,
which one was your favorite?

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:34.200
I like this one best.

00:13:34.200 --> 00:13:35.370
Go ahead.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:37.490
Are you just trying to flatter us?

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:39.700
I really mean it.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:41.910
Where are you from?

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:43.700
The Peaceful Country of Robetta.

00:13:43.700 --> 00:13:45.620
Is it fun being a traveler?

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:47.040
Yes, very!

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:50.540
I've got a question!
What about your panties? What color--

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:08.990
I instructed the students alongside Miss Fran.

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.660
The flow of your magic is going wild.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:16.740
Calm your mind more and stabilize your magic.

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:18.540
Yes, ma'am!

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:23.160
Hey, stop playing with making
your water into the shape of a sword.

00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:26.700
Miss Elaina.

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:29.740
I can't get my water to form a clean ball shape.

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:31.660
What should I do?

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:34.290
You're using too much excess magic.

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.830
Try relaxing your power a bit.

00:14:36.830 --> 00:14:38.370
Right.

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:40.910
Relax my power...

00:14:42.950 --> 00:14:45.990
You relaxed too much.

00:14:45.990 --> 00:14:50.040
U-Um... There's something
I'd like you to help me with.

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.410
Yes, what is it?

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:54.080
I'm bad at manipulating water...

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:56.990
I can barely lift it up...

00:14:56.990 --> 00:14:59.200
What should I do?

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:00.950
Please try doing it now.

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:02.370
Huh?

00:15:02.370 --> 00:15:04.450
Um, right...

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:12.830
Oh my.

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:15.450
What should I do?

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:18.540
It looks like you haven't quite
gotten the hang of it yet.

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:22.330
I think you should try practicing
just getting the water out first.

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:25.870
R-Right...

00:15:25.870 --> 00:15:27.950
Once you get the water out,

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:30.790
return it to the bucket right away.

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:33.330
And then pull it out again.

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:35.540
Do it like this.

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:37.120
I see.

00:15:37.120 --> 00:15:40.790
If you keep practicing this,
I think you'll start to get used to it.

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.370
R-Right...

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:44.540
Thank you very much!

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:45.740
No problem.

00:15:45.740 --> 00:15:46.660
Excuse me!

00:15:46.660 --> 00:15:48.580
Miss Elaina!

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:50.290
Look at this!

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:53.790
Isn't it cool?

00:15:53.790 --> 00:15:55.620
It's so cold!

00:15:55.620 --> 00:16:00.830
I don't usually teach things to other people,

00:16:00.830 --> 00:16:05.410
so with one thing and another,
I had a pretty good time.

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:48.790
This is my favorite spot.

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:55.580
I wanted to show you before
you left again on your journey.

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:57.870
I love this view.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:01.580
It really is a lovely view.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.580
You'll leave tomorrow morning, right?

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:05.870
Yes.

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:07.620
Too bad.

00:17:07.620 --> 00:17:11.240
I think the students really like you.

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:12.580
I'm sure they'll be sad.

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:15.490
It's just unusual to see a young witch.

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:19.660
Of course, I'll be sad, too.

00:17:19.660 --> 00:17:23.910
What will the students at the
academy do once they graduate?

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:25.950
They'll work.

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:27.910
Work?

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:29.120
Yes.

00:17:29.120 --> 00:17:32.790
Delivering packages, flying people around--

00:17:32.790 --> 00:17:34.580
There are many different jobs.

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:38.660
Are the street performers who use
magic also graduates of the academy?

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.330
Are they getting paid?

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:45.660
Not very much, but I'm sure they are.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:51.160
But you know, they're not showcasing
their magic because they want money.

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:54.450
Then why?

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:56.950
It's because they like it.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:01.790
I mean, you're traveling
because you like it, right?

00:18:01.790 --> 00:18:03.990
It's the same.

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:08.790
They're doing it because
they like making people happy.

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:11.700
Because they like it...

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:16.080
There were many times when I felt
that this was a wonderful country.

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:20.200
The beautiful streets, the smiling people...

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:23.950
I was moved every time I saw them.

00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:32.910
It could be that the country,
Royal Celesteria, overlapped with my journey.

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:36.740
Speaking of which,
what are some things you like?

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:39.450
Why are you asking that all of a sudden?

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:40.740
I like traveling.

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:43.740
Other than traveling.

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:45.160
I like books?

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:46.870
Anything else?

00:18:46.870 --> 00:18:48.950
What's this all about?

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:51.870
Nothing, I was just wondering.

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:54.740
Are you going to give me a parting gift?

00:18:54.740 --> 00:18:56.080
Yes, you could say that.

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:59.620
Oh, well, you don't need to do that.

00:18:59.620 --> 00:19:04.160
Don't say that. For example,
do you like flowers?

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:06.200
That's a leading question, isn't it?

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:08.080
Well, what about flowers?

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:10.540
Oh, butterflies are nice, too, aren't they?

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.950
That's what <i>you</i> like, Miss Fran.

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:16.700
You don't like butterflies?

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:18.540
They're okay.

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:21.290
I see. You like them okay.

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:23.620
So what about flowers, then?

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:25.200
Oh, you're back to flowers.

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:26.740
How about it?

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:29.120
Well, I do like them...

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:35.040
Okay, so you like flowers.
Let's meet at the city gates tomorrow.

00:19:39.870 --> 00:19:41.620
She's not here...

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:47.660
I thought, "Miss Fran is probably
planning on giving me flowers."

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.580
I'd be happy about that,

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:52.740
but flowers wouldn't last long.

00:19:52.740 --> 00:19:56.740
If I saw the same flowers in another country,

00:19:56.740 --> 00:20:00.040
I would remember Miss Fran and my time here,

00:20:00.040 --> 00:20:03.120
and it might make me sad.

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:08.790
I decided to leave on my journey
without waiting for Miss Fran.

00:20:08.790 --> 00:20:13.740
Because then, I might not have
to have those sad feelings later.

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:18.330
Goodbye, Miss Fran.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:29.160
A flower?

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:38.660
Elaina,

00:20:38.660 --> 00:20:44.660
you chose to become a traveler yourself,
so I don't have the right to stop you.

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:49.790
This is all I can do for you.

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:51.700
Miss Fran...

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:54.160
Did it make you happy?

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:58.830
Yes, very!

00:20:58.830 --> 00:21:03.200
The students and I are cheering
for you from the bottom of our hearts.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:05.370
Please do not forget that.

00:21:05.370 --> 00:21:09.040
I won't forget you all, either!

00:21:09.040 --> 00:21:11.740
G-Goodbye!

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:13.660
Make sure you come back and visit!

00:21:13.660 --> 00:21:15.790
We'll wait with open arms!

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:17.660
We'll be waiting for you.

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:19.580
Let us meet again someday.

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:23.410
Until then, goodbye.

00:21:23.410 --> 00:21:25.200
Yes!

00:21:30.410 --> 00:21:33.330
There is a witch flying over grasslands.

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:36.870
She looks excited, like she's having fun.

00:21:36.870 --> 00:21:39.700
What kind of country will she visit next?

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:42.410
What kinds of people will she meet next?

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:46.200
Her heart was filled with hope.

00:21:46.200 --> 00:21:49.540
Who was this traveler?

00:21:49.540 --> 00:21:52.990
Yes, it was me!

00:23:29.910 --> 00:23:33.950
Isn't that a little too cool-looking?

00:23:40.660 --> 00:23:43.370
It looks like the next time I see Miss Fran,

00:23:43.370 --> 00:23:47.950
I'll have a really
interesting story to tell her.
